Description: bzip2recover prints its block positions with %llu, not %Lu
 bzip2recover writes the 64-bit positions of the blocks it finds with the
 format "%Lu": "L" is the size of a long double in printf, and the
 combination is no conversion at all. glibc takes it as a long long; musl
 (which Jam OS uses) refuses it, and bzip2recover stops at the first block
 with "I/O error ... Invalid argument" before it has written a file.
Forwarded: not-needed (a one-line portability fix for musl; Jam OS has no fork to send it from)
---
--- a/bzip2recover.c
+++ b/bzip2recover.c
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 */
 #ifdef __GNUC__
    typedef  unsigned long long int  MaybeUInt64;
-#  define MaybeUInt64_FMT "%Lu"
+#  define MaybeUInt64_FMT "%llu"
 #else
 #ifdef _MSC_VER
    typedef  unsigned __int64  MaybeUInt64;
